{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.hecke_d_irrep_closed_form_character_g2_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.hecke_d_irrep_closed_form_character_g2_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L311-L321","doc":"**Conditional on `conj:borromean-quark`.** Under the Borromean\nhypothesis the total pairwise linking over the three colour tubes\nis zero: `Σ_{i,j} pairLink i j = 0`. Derived from the class field\n(every summand vanishes), not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.pairwise_unlinked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.pairwise_unlinked","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L308-L308","doc":"The three colour-tube constituents are pairwise unlinked:\nevery pairwise linking number vanishes (Borromean signature). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L305-L305","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke1dIrrepClosedFormCharacter.ConditionalAudit.BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L292-L309","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:borromean-quark`.\n\nA baryon is the Borromean link `𝓑₃` of three unknots\n(neutrinos `ν_r, ν_g, ν_b` in the three colour tubes) bound by the\nHopf link `𝓛_H`: `𝔭 = 𝓑₃(ν_r, ν_g, ν_b) ⊕ 𝓛_H`. The defining\nstructural feature is that the three constituents are *Borromean*:\npairwise unlinked, jointly linked.\n\nConcrete content (shape of the claim): a colour-indexed family\nof pairwise linking numbers `pairLink : Fin 3 → Fin 3 → ℤ` that\nvanishes on every pair (`pairLink i j = 0`) — the algebraic\nsignature of the Borromean property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.hecke_1d_irrep_closed_form_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.hecke_1d_irrep_closed_form_character","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L269-L283","doc":"**Universal 1-d Hecke irrep character closed form.** Combines the\ntrivial and sign specialisations into the canonical export. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character","label":"prop:hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.hecke_1d_sign_character_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.hecke_1d_sign_character_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L249-L259","doc":"**Sign-irrep character closed form.** For `λ_σ = -q⁻¹`,\n`χ_(1^n)_q(β) = (-q⁻¹)^w · (-[2]_q / 2)^m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.hecke_1d_trivial_character_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.hecke_1d_trivial_character_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L233-L243","doc":"**Trivial-irrep character closed form.** For `λ_σ = +q`,\n`χ_(n)_q(β) = q^w · ([2]_q / 2)^m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.oneDim_character_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.oneDim_character_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L164-L227","doc":"**Universal closed form for 1-d Hecke characters.** For any typed\nbraid `β` (list of crossing types) and any unit `λ_σ` (the two 1-d\nHecke eigenvalues are `+q` and `-q⁻¹`, both units),\n\n  `oneDimCharacter λ_σ q β = λ_σ^w · (λ_σ − h/2)^m`\n\nwhere `w = writhe β : ℤ` and `m = averagedCount β : ℕ`. The `ℤ`-power\nis the group power in `Rˣ`, so no nonvanishing side condition is\nneeded.\n\nThis is proved by induction on `β`; each step is a single application\nof `oneDimAction` and a power-arithmetic identity, both discharged\nby `ring` after the unfold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.sign_action_averaged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.sign_action_averaged","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L154-L160","doc":"Sign-irrep averaged action equals `-[2]_q / 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.trivial_action_averaged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.trivial_action_averaged","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L143-L148","doc":"Trivial-irrep averaged action equals `[2]_q / 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.trivial_action_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.trivial_action_plus","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L139-L141","doc":"Trivial-irrep crossing-action specialisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.oneDimCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.oneDimCharacter","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L123-L127","doc":"Multiplicative trace on a 1-d Hecke irrep over a typed braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.averagedCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.averagedCount","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L116-L121","doc":"Averaged-crossing count of a typed-braid encoding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.writhe","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L109-L114","doc":"Writhe of a typed-braid encoding: signed crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.oneDimAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.oneDimAction","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L101-L107","doc":"The 1-d action of a single typed crossing on a 1-d Hecke irrep with\ngenerator eigenvalue `λ_σ` (a unit of the base ring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.instReprCrossingType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.instReprCrossingType.repr","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.instReprCrossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.instReprCrossingType","kind":"instance","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.instDecidableEqCrossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.instDecidableEqCrossingType","kind":"instance","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType.Averaged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType.Averaged","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType.Minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType.Minus","kind":"ctor","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType.Plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType.Plus","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.CrossingType","kind":"inductive","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L95-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.qInt2_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.qInt2_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L71-L81","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical bracket.** The longhand `q + q⁻¹` is this site's\nbody and its proofs use it, so the consolidation is the identity, not an alias.\n\n`qInt2` above carries `q` as a **unit** over `CommRing`; the canonical\n`qIntBal` is a guarded division and stays over a field, so the bridge is where\nthe two meet. Conditional: they agree away from `q − q⁻¹ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.qInt2","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L67-L68","doc":"Quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke1dIrrep.heckeH","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-1d-irrep-closed-form-character.lean#L64-L65","doc":"Quantum-integer differential `h(q) = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}